   <refbody class="- topic/body        reference/refbody " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="refbody:1;24:13">    <section class="- topic/section " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="section:1;24:26">
      <p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="p:1;25:10">This section describes the parameters used to assess the condition of a motor component.</p>
      <p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="p:2;26:10">Each parameter in the following table represents the Fault Score Index (FSI) of the corresponding motor component condition. These predicted health indicators for motor components are generated each time the analytics processes data samples received from a running motor. The values are between zero and ten:</p>
      <ul id="ul_10211554" class="- topic/ul " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="ul:1;27:28">
         <li class="- topic/li " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="li:1;28:14">A value of 10 corresponds to a perfect state for the component.</li>
         <li class="- topic/li " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="li:2;29:14">A value of 0 corresponds to a catastrophic state for the component.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1" class="- topic/table " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="table:1;32:42">
