                  <entry class="- topic/entry " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="entry:28;108:26">
                     <codeblock xml:space="preserve" class="+ topic/pre pr-d/codeblock " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="codeblock:9;109:54">motorStructure</codeblock>
                  </entry>
                  <entry class="- topic/entry " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="entry:29;111:26">Loose Foot</entry>
                  <entry class="- topic/entry " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="entry:30;112:26">Structural looseness occurring when the motor base (or connection to the motor base) is not properly tightened.</entry>
               </row>
               <row class="- topic/row " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="row:11;114:21">
                  <entry class="- topic/entry " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="entry:31;115:26">
                     <codeblock xml:space="preserve" class="+ topic/pre pr-d/codeblock " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="codeblock:10;116:54">performance</codeblock>
                  </entry>
                  <entry class="- topic/entry " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="entry:32;118:26">Performance</entry>
                  <entry class="- topic/entry " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/appendices/conditions.dita" xtrc="entry:33;119:26">Used to capture abnormal events such as an overall increase in vibrations, unusual changes in motor RPM, motor load or temperatures, etc. Indicates faults that do not correspond to any of the other nine fault categories, which could be related to machine process.</entry>
